-- title:
--   The chosen diagonal-cover slot encoding is injective
-- statement:
--   Let $N>0$, $r\in\mathbb N$, and $A\subseteq\mathbb Z/N\mathbb Z$ be finite. For any deleted-face family covering all labelled simplices of the $(r+2)$-colour AP hypergraph of $A$, the canonical map from a diagonal parameter in $A\times(\mathbb Z/N\mathbb Z)^r$ to its chosen deleted colour and ordered deleted-face tuple is injective. Distinct diagonal parameters therefore occupy distinct coloured deletion slots.
